-Critical checks: State learner knowledge; apply the uniform two-world prior carefully; avoid claiming fixed-law necessity.
+## 4. Formalize the hidden-terminal lower-bound atom
+Goal: Turn the interval-world construction into a theorem with exact quantifiers and proof:
+\[
+\Gamma=
+\frac12(\sup_a g_0(a)+\sup_a g_1(a))
+-\sup_a\frac{g_0(a)+g_1(a)}2.
+\]
+If two laws are observationally identical for \(D\) rounds and have Bayes gap \(\Gamma\), minimax regret is at least \(D\Gamma\).
+Why promising: It captures the real lower-bound mechanism: valuable delayed reward plus indistinguishability.
+Critical checks: Keep it finite-horizon/class-level unless a separate infinite-process argument is proved.
 
